      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-11-01T17:26:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To the casual observer, it looks like you\u0027re lazily initializing the state machine for no obvious reason.  Could you call out why you\u0027re not just instantiating the state machine in the constructor with this comment?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 130,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 130,
        "endChar": 76
      },
      "revId": "a7ef211f45e23c332a80c21fe87dec70a99cceea",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8bb2e3c3_afe83a3a",
        "filename": "service/java/com/android/server/wifi/WifiStateMachinePrime.java",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 130,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-11-07T19:37:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As above, I am only creating the state machine when we get a mode command.  This allows us to avoid creating the state machine if we will never need it.",
      "parentUuid": "810004b4_0c2e4758",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 130,
        "startChar": 15,
